## Add index to dataframe

To add an index to a Polars dataframe, use the `with_row_index` method like this:

::: {#645a2af1 .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
df.with_row_index()
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (8, 3)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>index</th><th>Student</th><th>Subject</th></tr><tr><td>u32</td><td>str</td><td>str</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0</td><td>&quot;Spencer&quot;</td><td>&quot;Chemistry&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>&quot;Spencer&quot;</td><td>&quot;Physics&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>&quot;Emily&quot;</td><td>&quot;Physics&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>&quot;Emily&quot;</td><td>&quot;Biology&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>&quot;Hannah&quot;</td><td>&quot;History&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>&quot;Hannah&quot;</td><td>&quot;Art&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>&quot;Aria&quot;</td><td>&quot;English&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>&quot;Aria&quot;</td><td>&quot;Biology&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


<br>
Notice that the index starts at zero. If you want it to start at a different number, such as 1, you can add the `offset` parameter like this:

::: {#759f0aa6 .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
df.with_row_index(offset=1)
```

